{
  "id": "mark-vs-wiggle-bigwig",
  "measured": "2026-09-17",
  "published": false,
  "source": {
    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "node plugins/marks/benches/bigwigPaths.bench.ts, then the same with --file=<a coverage BigWig> --start=10000000 for the second file (CD16_Mono.bw is a 10x scRNA cluster coverage track over hg38, local to the machine that measured)",
    "notes": "One 1500 px screen per zoom, from the contig start, at one bp/px inside each of the file's tiers, the adapter's synthetic tiers included (ADR-129), and one in its raw section; `tier` is the reduction level the adapter reads at that zoom. wiggle is getFeatureArraysMulti plus processFeaturesFromArrays, the RenderWiggleData executor's work for the region; marks is getFeaturesArray plus encodeFeatures over the bar shape's lanes, the CoreEncodeFeatures executor's work for `{ mark: 'bar', encoding: { y: 'score' } }`, so the difference is the BigWigFeature objects, the rxjs collect and the hover index; marks-mean runs `bin: auto` and `aggregate: mean` on top. control is the wiggle arm declared a second time. Interleaved round-robin, MIN across rounds, bbi's block cache warm after the first round: a refetch across a tier, not a cold open. The error columns are `aggregate: mean` over `bin: auto` of the tier's rows against the raw section's coverage-weighted mean over the same bins, as a percentage of the raw score range on the screen: unweighted is what the encoder computes, since bbi exports no validCnt; span-weighted is what a validCnt-weighted mean would approach on data this dense."
  },
